# Deploy Micro-Hub changes into the game

When a change in this repo affects a plugin or the setup GUI, finish by installing it. Do not leave the update only in source.

1. Build the changed plugin jar into `dist/`. The task name is the plugin class plus `Jar`, for example `gradlew BankSorterPluginJar --offline`. Use `gradlew build` only when several plugins or `dist/library.txt` changed. Skip plugins that fail for an unrelated missing dependency.
2. Copy each new jar from `dist/<Name>.jar` to `%USERPROFILE%\.runelite\microbot-plugins\<Name>.jar`. That folder is what Microbot loads. The setup GUI (`installer/OpraMicroHub-Setup.bat`) reads the same `dist/` jars, so the build updates the GUI list too.
3. If Windows has the jar locked, ask Dani to close the client, then copy again. A running client keeps the old plugin until it is restarted.
4. Tell Dani the jar was copied and that the client must be restarted before the change is in game.
